WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.168 --> 00:00:22.363
"What do you mean?" Zann asked Gliss. "What did you find out while you were a prisoner?"

2
00:00:22.364 --> 00:00:24.998
"Is it something about Morb?" Darb asked.

3
00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:30.469
Gliss' lower lip trembled. "Yes," she said. "And it's horrible!"

4
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.030
"Tell us," Perda urged.

5
00:00:33.031 --> 00:00:38.564
"A few of the other Reds understood the trolls' language," Gliss said.

6
00:00:38.565 --> 00:00:41.866
"They listened when our guards talked to one another.

7
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:48.543
The trolls kept grumbling about having to keep us at the zoo instead of zapping us back to Morb's fortress."

8
00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:51.506
"We were wondering about that too," Darb said.

9
00:00:51.507 --> 00:00:58.585
Zann nodded. "We guessed it might be because Morb used up all his power kidnapping the king and queen."

10
00:00:58.586 --> 00:01:05.299
"That's not why," Gliss said. "Kidnapping the king and queen gave Morb even more power.

11
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:12.542
He left the trolls alone because he's busy building a horrible machine to steal all of the magical energy in Magica!"

12
00:01:12.543 --> 00:01:16.510
Perda gasped. "What? That's impossible!"

13
00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:19.706
"That's what I thought at first," Gliss said.

14
00:01:19.707 --> 00:01:24.939
"I figured the trolls must be confused. Everyone knows they're pretty dumb.

15
00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.066
But then I talked to a woman named Saffa."

16
00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:34.156
"She's one of Boz's Magic Master friends," Zann said. "What did she say?"

17
00:01:34.157 --> 00:01:39.151
"Saffa knows about an ancient text from the Old Times," Gliss replied.

18
00:01:39.152 --> 00:01:43.146
"It contains plans for building a machine that could do what the trolls said—

19
00:01:43.147 --> 00:01:50.189
suck the power out of Reds, regular people, dragons, message moths, mood trees, whatever.

20
00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:53.993
Anything or anyone with any magic at all."

21
00:01:53.994 --> 00:02:02.050
Zann gulped. "So if Morb succeeded in building this machine, he would control all the magic in Magica?"

22
00:02:02.051 --> 00:02:06.924
Gliss nodded. "Saffa said the Old Times ended because of that machine.

23
00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:14.712
An extremely powerful and evil magician invented it, and when people realized what the machine could do, they were shocked.

24
00:02:14.713 --> 00:02:23.303
People decided no one person should have that much power, and that Magica needed laws to protect the weak from the strong."

25
00:02:23.304 --> 00:02:27.341
"That was when the first Red Council was formed," Darb put in.

26
00:02:27.342 --> 00:02:30.869
"The first thing the members did was enact the Days of Discipline.

27
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.429
I've read a lot about that—but I've never heard of the magic-sucking machine."

28
00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:40.001
"How could Morb get his hands on those plans?" Zann wondered.

29
00:02:40.002 --> 00:02:44.669
"Teplo says all the ancient texts are locked away at the university."

30
00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:51.938
"Saffa suspects there's another copy of the text hidden deep within the Cave of the Unknown," Gliss said.

31
00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:55.144
"How would Morb have found it?" Perda asked.

32
00:02:55.145 --> 00:03:00.084
"Even the most powerful Magic Masters don't dare go too deep in there."

33
00:03:00.085 --> 00:03:04.163
Gliss shrugged. "Who knows? But if he did . . ."

34
00:03:04.164 --> 00:03:06.016
Her voice trailed off.

35
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:09.389
For a moment the kids all stared at one another in silence.

36
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.046
Zann was the first to speak. "We have to warn somebody.

37
00:03:13.047 --> 00:03:18.245
If this is true, Morb needs to be stopped before it's too late."

38
00:03:18.246 --> 00:03:20.787
"Let's go to the palace," Perda said.

39
00:03:20.788 --> 00:03:23.830
"Yog will be able to get word to Venna from there."

40
00:03:23.831 --> 00:03:28.548
"Wait!" Gliss broke in. "Let's just wait for Fala to get back.

41
00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:32.101
She's not a Red—it's safer for her to go."

42
00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:38.860
"But if Morb really is working on this magic-sucking machine, there's no time to waste!" Perda said.

43
00:03:38.861 --> 00:03:45.997
Zann knew that Perda was right. But he still felt guilty about convincing Gliss to zap out of the palace earlier.

44
00:03:45.998 --> 00:03:49.744
He didn't want to talk her into something else that could be dangerous.

45
00:03:49.745 --> 00:03:53.648
"Why don't you stay here while the rest of us go?" he suggested.

46
00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:56.019
"You can tell Fala where we went."

47
00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.504
"No!" Gliss said. "If you're all going, I'm going too."

48
00:04:00.505 --> 00:04:07.992
"Okay," Zann agreed. Obviously Gliss didn't want to be alone.

49
00:04:07.993 --> 00:04:11.407
It didn't take long for Zann and his friends to reach the palace.

50
00:04:11.408 --> 00:04:16.013
A stout man with a bristly brown beard was standing guard at the main entrance.

51
00:04:16.014 --> 00:04:22.607
"No visitors," he said without even looking at the kids. "Official business only today."

52
00:04:22.608 --> 00:04:26.461
"We are here on official business," Perda said.

53
00:04:26.462 --> 00:04:29.634
"We need to talk to Yog. Or Rixa."

54
00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:34.966
The guard glanced at her, looking skeptical. "What's your business?"

55
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:40.073
"Please, just tell Yog or Rixa that we're here," Zann said.

56
00:04:40.074 --> 00:04:43.985
The guard's jaw dropped as he noticed Zann's hair color.

57
00:04:43.986 --> 00:04:49.297
"Reds!" he exclaimed. "What did you say your names were again?"

58
00:04:49.298 --> 00:04:53.485
Zann and his friends waited impatiently while the guard sent a message moth.

59
00:04:53.486 --> 00:04:56.486
Soon the moth returned with a new message.

60
00:04:56.487 --> 00:05:00.394
The guard read it. "Rixa says to let you in.

61
00:05:00.395 --> 00:05:03.818
You'll find her in the throne room with Slib."

62
00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:07.279
Zann wondered if that meant Slib had taken over the government.

63
00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:16.755
"Thanks," he said. He and his friends hurried inside before the guard could change his mind about letting them in.

64
00:05:16.756 --> 00:05:21.678
Then they stopped. "Do you remember how to get to the throne room?" Gliss asked.

65
00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:25.724
"How could I? We crawled in through a tunnel and zapped out."

66
00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:30.152
Perda glanced up and down the hallway. "Wait, is that it?"

67
00:05:30.153 --> 00:05:34.791
The kids could see a large, arched doorway farther down the hall, and they hurried to it.

68
00:05:34.792 --> 00:05:38.173
Zann peered in and saw a large crowd of adults.

69
00:05:38.174 --> 00:05:41.484
"Do you see Rixa or Yog?" Gliss whispered.

70
00:05:41.485 --> 00:05:46.056
Zann couldn't see Yog anywhere. But he spotted Rixa arguing with Slib.

71
00:05:46.057 --> 00:05:50.248
Before he could point her out, a burst of magical energy filled the room.

72
00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:57.227
Morb appeared in front of the thrones—along with half a dozen trolls and a cloud of tiny, buzzing dragons.

73
00:05:57.228 --> 00:06:00.488
Thinking fast, Zann pulled his friends out of sight.

74
00:06:00.489 --> 00:06:05.031
His heart pounded with fear. Had Morb tracked them here somehow?

75
00:06:05.032 --> 00:06:07.573
Morb didn't even glance in their direction though.

76
00:06:07.574 --> 00:06:10.642
He stared at the stunned adults with a smile.

77
00:06:10.643 --> 00:06:16.455
"Hello again," he said. "I liked it here so much that I decided to return."

78
00:06:16.456 --> 00:06:19.668
He stepped over to the king's throne and sat down.

79
00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:26.582
"And this time I think I'll stay."
